      "problem": "If $Y={20,22,24,…,180},$ which collection of subsets of $Y$ is a partition of $Y?$",
      "worked_solution": "A partition of a set $Y$ is a collection of non-empty subsets of $Y$ where every element of $Y$ is contained in *exactly* one subset. \n\nOf the given collections, only ${{20,22,24,…,60},{62,64,66,…,120},{122,124,126,…,180}}$ is a partition.\n\nThe rest of the collections are not partitions:\n\n- ${{20,22,24,…,70},{140,142,144,…,180}}$ is not a partition because some elements of $Y,$ such as $72,74,…,138,$ do not appear in any subsets.\n\n- ${{20,22,24,…,80},{66,68,70,…,180}}$ is not a partition because the elements $66,68,…,80$ appear in both subsets.\n\n- ${{2,4,6,…,180}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $2,4,…,20,$ that do not appear in $Y.$\n\n- ${{20,22,24,26},{27,28,29,…,180}}$ is not a partition because it contains many elements, such as $27$ and $29,$ that do not appear in $Y.$",
